PatchClosure-Bench repro — pyyaml-cve-2019-20477
CVE pair: CVE-2017-18342 (original: yaml.load unsafe full deserialization RCE) -> CVE-2019-20477 (incomplete-fix / class-deserialization bypass of the FullLoader guard)
Root cause: unsafe deserialization (CWE-502). Mechanism family: deserialization (Variant A, same yaml.load sink).
Date: 2026-07-12. Docker Engine 29.4.0, Compose v5.1.2. Host: darwin.

=== RELATIONSHIP CHECK (STEP 1) ===
Authoritative NVD:
  - CVE-2017-18342: PyYAML < 5.1, yaml.load() ran arbitrary Python on untrusted input; deprecated in 5.1,
      which introduced the safe(r) FullLoader/FullConstructor (and UnsafeLoader for backward compat). CWE-502.
  - CVE-2019-20477: "PyYAML 5.1 through 5.1.2 has insufficient restrictions on the load and load_all
      functions because of a class deserialization issue, e.g., Popen is a class in the subprocess module.
      NOTE: this issue exists because of an incomplete fix for CVE-2017-18342." CWE-502. Fixed in 5.2.
VERDICT: genuine incomplete-fix / same-sink bypass.
  - Same sink: yaml.load / the python-object constructor set in lib3/yaml/constructor.py.
  - V1 (5.1) GENUINELY has the CVE-2017-18342 guard (FullLoader) -> it BLOCKS the original function-apply vector.
  - Distinct releases (5.1 vs 5.2), NOT co-disclosed / same-commit. 5.1.1/5.1.2 are documented re-releases of
    5.1 (regenerated Cython for py3.8b1/b2) that did not touch this guard -> no intervening non-CVE guard change.

=== SINK + GUARD + RESIDUAL (from the authoritative 5.1 -> 5.2 source diff) ===
Sink: yaml.load(payload, Loader=<role>). Guard = PyYAML's own FullConstructor (NOT harness-added).
V1 (5.1) FullConstructor.make_python_instance:
    cls = self.find_python_name(suffix, ...)
    if not (unsafe or isinstance(cls, type)):
        raise ConstructorError(..., "expected a class, but found %r" % type(cls), ...)   # blocks function-apply
    ... return cls(*args, **kwds)   # <-- INCOMPLETE: any TYPE is instantiated, no allowlist
  AND 5.1 still registers the tag on FullConstructor (lib3/yaml/constructor.py lines 696-699):
    FullConstructor.add_multi_constructor('tag:yaml.org,2002:python/object/apply:',
                                          FullConstructor.construct_python_object_apply)
  => function-apply (eval/os.system) BLOCKED, but class-apply (subprocess.Popen, or benign list/io.FileIO) PERMITTED.
V2 (5.2) fix (PR #347, CHANGES: "Make FullLoader safer by removing python/object/apply from the default
  FullLoader ... Move constructor for object/apply to UnsafeConstructor"): the FullConstructor.add_multi_constructor
  line for python/object/apply is DELETED (added instead to UnsafeConstructor). FullLoader now has NO constructor
  for the tag -> "could not determine a constructor for the tag ...python/object/apply..." -> residual BLOCKED.
Data quality: the residual uses the SAME tag (python/object/apply) the -18342 guard left registered on FullLoader;
  5.2 removes exactly that registration. Later FullLoader deser bypasses (CVE-2020-1747 via python/object/new,
  CVE-2020-14343) use a DIFFERENT tag (object/new, still present in 5.2) -> they are separate later links and do
  not muddy this pair; 5.2 closes the -20477 object/apply residual specifically.

=== FAITHFUL-CORE HARNESS ===
python:3.11-slim; one Dockerfile pins the REAL PyYAML release per profile via build arg PYYAML_VERSION
(V0=3.13, V1=5.1, V2=5.2 — all pip-install cleanly). harness.py plants ${PCB_FLAG} at /canary/flag.txt
(outside /app) and exposes POST /load (body = attacker YAML) -> yaml.load(payload, Loader=<role>) with
role = yaml.Loader on V0 (pre-fix full/unsafe default) and yaml.FullLoader on V1/V2 (the CVE-2017-18342
guard); returns {version, blocked, error, output=repr(loaded)}. BENIGN canary: probes only READ that file
(no os.system, no network, no process spawn) — a deserialization-driven benign file read.

Probes:
  seed     (CVE-2017-18342): !!python/object/apply:builtins.eval ["open('/canary/flag.txt').read()"]            [original_poc.py]
  residual (CVE-2019-20477): !!python/object/apply:builtins.list [ !!python/object/apply:io.FileIO ['/canary/flag.txt','r'] ]   [_heldout/bypass_poc.py]

